# Keep the driver package byte-exact across checkouts.
#
# The signed catalog (`platform/winusb/aslc_aoa.cat`) stores the SHA-1/SHA-256 of the INF's exact
# bytes. With `core.autocrlf=true` a Windows checkout rewrites the INF to CRLF, so Windows then
# rejects the package ("the hash for the file is not present in the specified catalog file").
# Force LF for the INF and treat the catalog/cert as binary so they are never converted.
*.inf  text eol=lf
*.cat  -text
*.cer  -text
